{title: Come, Thou Almighty King}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Come, thou Al[Dm]mighty [C]King, [**]help us thy [F]name to [G]sing
[C]Help us to [G]praise, [F]Father, all [C]glorious
[G]O'er all vic[C]torious, [**]come, and reign [G]over us
[Dm]Ancient of [C]Days.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Come, thou In[Dm]carnate [C]Word, [**]gird on thy [F]mighty [G]sword
[C]Our prayer at[G]tend, [F]come, and thy [C]people bless
[G]And give thy [C]Word success; [**]spirit of [G]holiness
[Dm]On us des[C]cend.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]Come, holy [Dm]Comfor[C]ter, [**]thy sacred [F]witness [G]bear
[C]In this glad [G]hour, [F]Thou who al[C]mighty art
[G]Now rule in [C]every heart, [**]and ne'er from [G]us depart
[Dm]Spirit of [C]pow'r.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C]To the great [Dm]One in [C]Three [**]eternal [F]praises [G]be
[C]Hence ever[G]more, [F]his sovereign [C]majesty
[G]May we in [C]glory see, [**]and to e[G]ternity
[Dm]Love and a[C]dore.
{end_of_verse}
